# Cloudflare Pages security headers.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the build output; files in
# apps/web/public/ are copied to dist/ at build time, so this lands at dist/_headers.
# (Cloudflare Pages ignores vercel.json — these headers replace the ones defined
# there, which were never applied on the live Cloudflare-served site.)
#
# CSP NOTE: the policy below whitelists Google Tag Manager + the common campaign
# stack (GA4, Google Ads, Meta Pixel) + the Cookiebot consent banner. Any OTHER
# tag type added later via GTM (e.g. LinkedIn Insight, TikTok Pixel, Hotjar)
# loads from a domain not listed here and will be silently BLOCKED until its
# domain is added below. Because the client manages tags in GTM but cannot edit
# this repo, route any new tag types through the dev/agency so the CSP can be
# updated.
#
# GOOGLE ADS: conversion tracking + remarketing domains follow
# https://developers.google.com/tag-platform/security/guides/csp —
# googleadservices.com, *.doubleclick.net, pagead2.googlesyndication.com and
# google.com/google.co.uk. Google's docs specify `www.google.<TLD>` for the
# country-level ping (ga-audiences); only .com and .co.uk are listed here, so
# visitors browsing from a non-UK Google TLD may drop that one remarketing ping.
# Add further TLDs here if Ads reports gaps.
#
# !! 2,000 CHARACTER LIMIT - READ BEFORE EDITING THE CSP !!
# Cloudflare Pages enforces a 2,000 character limit on each LINE of this file
# (name + value + indentation). A line over the limit is dropped SILENTLY: the
# build still succeeds, the deploy still reports green, and the header simply
# stops being served. This already happened once — the CSP hit 2,055 chars and
# the live site served no CSP at all until it was shortened.
#
# The CSP line is currently ~1,690 chars. Before pushing any CSP change, check:
#
#   awk '/^  Content-Security-Policy:/ { print length($0) }' apps/web/public/_headers
#
# and confirm the live header actually survives after deploy:
#
#   curl -sSI https://marrlaserandskinclinic.com/ | grep -i content-security-policy
#
# If you need room, consolidate same-vendor hosts into one wildcard rather than
# dropping sources — `https://*.doubleclick.net` covers googleads.g / stats.g /
# td / ad, and CSP host wildcards match multi-level subdomains. Splitting the
# policy across two lines does NOT work: Cloudflare comma-joins duplicate
# headers, and browsers treat that as two policies that must BOTH pass, which is
# stricter than intended and will break tracking.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: payment=(self "https://www.phorest.com")
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://tagmanager.google.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://www.google.com https://connect.facebook.net https://elfsightcdn.com https://*.elfsight.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://*.cookiebot.com https://fonts.googleapis.com https://tagmanager.google.com https://*.elfsight.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.googleadservices.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://www.google.com https://google.com https://www.google.co.uk https://www.facebook.com https://cdn.sanity.io https://img.youtube.com https://*.cdninstagram.com https://*.fbcdn.net https://*.elfsightcdn.com data:; frame-src https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://www.phorest.com https://phorest.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://*.elfsight.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; connect-src 'self' https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://tagmanager.google.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.googleadservices.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://www.google.com https://google.com https://www.google.co.uk https://connect.facebook.net https://www.facebook.com https://*.sanity.io https://*.elfsight.com https://elfsightcdn.com
